<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines sees higher coconut output in 1997.</title>
<headline>Philippines sees higher coconut output in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Coconut Authority (PCA) said on Monday it sees 1997 coconut production at 2.6 million tonnes compared with 2.4 million in 1996.</p>
<p>PCA Administrator Virgilio David told a news conference that improved weather conditions will raise the country's coconut production.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect production to pick up starting the second quarter of the year,&quot; David said.</p>
<p>David said that by the year 2000, coconut production is expected to reach 3.0 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The Philippines is the world's largest exporter of coconut products.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 8418939 Fax 8176267</p>
